            <div class="col s12 m8 paragraphStyleNews">
                <p>
                    ‘Rock, Paper, Scissors’ has just premiered on Vilpa Max with a runtime of 20min and 53 seconds. The
                    film, which is based on true events, won the 2025 BAFTA for Best British Short Film and is currently
                    shortlisted for the Academy Awards in the Live Action Short Film Category.
                </p>
                <p>
                    The film follows Ivan, a young man hiding in a hospital’s bunker in eastern Ukraine. He is
                    accompanied by his father and other hospital visitors as they await evacuation. However, when their
                    evacuation vehicle is destroyed by Russian aviation, they receive word that Russian soldiers are
                    approaching the bunker they are hiding in. How Ivan decides to fight back against the approaching
                    army is a choice that will irrevocably change both the lives of the others hiding with him, and his
                    own.
                </p>
                <p>
                    ‘Rock, Paper, Scissors’ is an emotionally charged story, and atmospheric in terms of its pacing.
                    Viewers feel drawn to the portrayal of Ivan, especially his terror when seeing the Russian soldiers
                    and later confronting them. With the film being based on a true story, it becomes even more of an
                    emotional impact and leaves viewers devastated.
                </p>
                <p>
                    The film features an outstanding cast, including Jonathan Tucker as Jeffrey, Bashy as Jaydee, and
                    Jackson Robert Scott as Troy, best known for playing Georgie in the IT film franchise.
                </p>
                <p>
                    The film stars a notable cast, including Oleksandr Rudynskyi as Ivan, who received the title of
                    Merited Artist of Ukraine in 2025. His performance as Ivan feels realistic and raw, showcasing the
                    real scenario of a young teenager being forcibly thrust into dangerous settings out of his control.
                </p>

